{"id":"msg-1770080976410-y6xtvn","type":"tool","content":"     1→# Stacks\n     2→\n     3→AI-powered infinite canvas workspace for notes, images, and creative organization.\n     4→\n     5→Free to use for personal use, one-time license of $49 for unrestricted usage - bit.ly/4aNe23d\n     6→\n     7→Please consider a license\n     8→\n     9→## Features\n    10→\n    11→- Infinite canvas with zoom and pan\n    12→- Notes, sticky notes, and text items\n    13→- Image support with EXIF metadata\n    14→- AI-powered organization and analysis\n    15→- Connect items with visual links\n    16→- Auto-arrange with ELK layout engine\n    17→- Auto-save to local storage\n    18→- MCP server for AI integration\n    19→\n    20→## Installation\n    21→\n    22→### Run with npx (no installation)\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→npx stacks-ai\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→On first run, Electron will be downloaded automatically (~100MB). Subsequent runs are instant.\n    29→\n    30→### Install globally\n    31→\n    32→```bash\n    33→npm install -g stacks-ai\n    34→stacks-ai\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→### Install from source\n    38→\n    39→```bash\n    40→git clone https://github.com/jasonkneen/stacks.git\n    41→cd stacks\n    42→npm install\n    43→npm run build\n    44→npm run electron\n    45→```\n    46→\n    47→## Development\n    48→\n    49→```bash\n    50→# Install dependencies\n    51→npm install\n    52→\n    53→# Run dev server (web only)\n    54→npm run dev\n    55→\n    56→# Run Electron in dev mode\n    57→npm run electron:dev\n    58→\n    59→# Build for production\n    60→npm run build:prod\n    61→\n    62→# Run MCP server\n    63→npm run mcp:dev\n    64→```\n    65→\n    66→## Environment Variables\n    67→\n    68→Create a `.env` file in the root directory:\n    69→\n    70→```env\n    71→GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here\n    72→```\n    73→\n    74→## Package Structure\n    75→\n    76→- `bin/` - CLI launcher script\n    77→- `electron/` - Electron main process\n    78→- `dist/` - Built application assets\n    79→- `mcp/` - Model Context Protocol server\n    80→\n    81→## How it works\n    82→\n    83→When you run `npx stacks-ai` or `stacks-ai`:\n    84→\n    85→1. The launcher script checks if Electron is installed\n    86→2. If not, it downloads Electron (~100MB, cached in `~/.stacks/`)\n    87→3. The MCP proxy starts for AI integration\n    88→4. Electron loads the built app from `dist/`\n    89→5. The app runs entirely locally - no internet required (except for AI features)\n    90→\n    91→## License\n    92→\n    93→**Stacks Community License v1.0**\n    94→\n    95→- **Personal Use**: Free to use, modify, and distribute for personal, non-commercial purposes\n    96→- **Open Source Distribution**: Free to fork, rebrand, and publish under a different name, provided it remains open source under this same license\n    97→- **Commercial Use**: Requires a one-time license fee of $49 USD. Commercial use includes any use within a business, for-profit organization, or any revenue-generating activity. Purchase at [bit.ly/4aNe23d](http://bit.ly/4aNe23d)\n    98→\n    99→Commercial license grants unrestricted use of the code for your business.\n   100→\n   101→See [LICENSE](LICENSE) for full terms.\n   102→\n   103→## Author\n   104→\n   105→Jason Kneen\n   106→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n","timestamp":1770080976410,"toolName":"Read","toolUseId":"toolu_017kV6Mk3MTs3otkffhA4qL5","toolInput":{"file_path":"/Users/jkneen/Documents/GitHub/spatial/README.md"},"toolResult":"     1→# Stacks\n     2→\n     3→AI-powered infinite canvas workspace for notes, images, and creative organization.\n     4→\n     5→Free to use for personal use, one-time license of $49 for unrestricted usage - bit.ly/4aNe23d\n     6→\n     7→Please consider a license\n     8→\n     9→## Features\n    10→\n    11→- Infinite canvas with zoom and pan\n    12→- Notes, sticky notes, and text items\n    13→- Image support with EXIF metadata\n    14→- AI-powered organization and analysis\n    15→- Connect items with visual links\n    16→- Auto-arrange with ELK layout engine\n    17→- Auto-save to local storage\n    18→- MCP server for AI integration\n    19→\n    20→## Installation\n    21→\n    22→### Run with npx (no installation)\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→npx stacks-ai\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→On first run, Electron will be downloaded automatically (~100MB). Subsequent runs are instant.\n    29→\n    30→### Install globally\n    31→\n    32→```bash\n    33→npm install -g stacks-ai\n    34→stacks-ai\n    35→```\n    36→\n    37→### Install from source\n    38→\n    39→```bash\n    40→git clone https://github.com/jasonkneen/stacks.git\n    41→cd stacks\n    42→npm install\n    43→npm run build\n    44→npm run electron\n    45→```\n    46→\n    47→## Development\n    48→\n    49→```bash\n    50→# Install dependencies\n    51→npm install\n    52→\n    53→# Run dev server (web only)\n    54→npm run dev\n    55→\n    56→# Run Electron in dev mode\n    57→npm run electron:dev\n    58→\n    59→# Build for production\n    60→npm run build:prod\n    61→\n    62→# Run MCP server\n    63→npm run mcp:dev\n    64→```\n    65→\n    66→## Environment Variables\n    67→\n    68→Create a `.env` file in the root directory:\n    69→\n    70→```env\n    71→GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here\n    72→```\n    73→\n    74→## Package Structure\n    75→\n    76→- `bin/` - CLI launcher script\n    77→- `electron/` - Electron main process\n    78→- `dist/` - Built application assets\n    79→- `mcp/` - Model Context Protocol server\n    80→\n    81→## How it works\n    82→\n    83→When you run `npx stacks-ai` or `stacks-ai`:\n    84→\n    85→1. The launcher script checks if Electron is installed\n    86→2. If not, it downloads Electron (~100MB, cached in `~/.stacks/`)\n    87→3. The MCP proxy starts for AI integration\n    88→4. Electron loads the built app from `dist/`\n    89→5. The app runs entirely locally - no internet required (except for AI features)\n    90→\n    91→## License\n    92→\n    93→**Stacks Community License v1.0**\n    94→\n    95→- **Personal Use**: Free to use, modify, and distribute for personal, non-commercial purposes\n    96→- **Open Source Distribution**: Free to fork, rebrand, and publish under a different name, provided it remains open source under this same license\n    97→- **Commercial Use**: Requires a one-time license fee of $49 USD. Commercial use includes any use within a business, for-profit organization, or any revenue-generating activity. Purchase at [bit.ly/4aNe23d](http://bit.ly/4aNe23d)\n    98→\n    99→Commercial license grants unrestricted use of the code for your business.\n   100→\n   101→See [LICENSE](LICENSE) for full terms.\n   102→\n   103→## Author\n   104→\n   105→Jason Kneen\n   106→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n","toolStatus":"completed","toolDisplayMeta":{"displayName":"Read","category":"native"},"isError":false,"turnId":"msg_019ygscqHvzpqAr79iV7SXva"}
